In the US, antitrust laws are enforced by the Federal Trade Commission (FTC) and state antitrust authorities. The FTC has the power to investigate and prosecute companies that engage in antitrust activities, such as mergers, acquisitions, and price fixing. The FTC also has the authority to fine companies up to $2 billion for violating antitrust laws.
